<!--
	Roaming fake players (see config/Custom/FakePlayerPvp.ini).

	kit: gear worn by a fake player. Each tier is used from its minLevel until the next tier
	     (1 = no grade, 20 = D, 40 = C, 52 = B, 61 = A, 76 = S, 80 = S80, 84 = S84).
	     Stats are read from the item data, so any item id can be used.

	buffs: buffs a fake player keeps on itself, like a player coming from the buffer.
	     Tiers add up: a level 76 fighter gets the 1, 40, 61 and 76 lists. Format: id,level;id,level
	     Buffs sharing an abnormal type (e.g. Chant of Victory, Magnus' Chant and the Prophecies,
	     or Greater Might and Greater Shield) overwrite each other, so list only one of them.

	build: a class a fake player can be.
	     classId - the final (3rd) class; below 76 the matching 2nd/1st/base class is used.
	     role    - FIGHTER, TANK, DAGGER (melee), ARCHER (keeps distance) or MAGE (casts and kites).
	     buffs   - buff list to use, default MAGE for mystic classes and FIGHTER for the others.
	     bow     - kit of a bow it carries besides its weapon (tanks, tyrants). It takes the bow out against
	               a player it can't catch and switches back to its weapon (and shield) when the player comes
	               close (see FakePvpWeaponSwap* in config/Custom/FakePlayerPvp.ini).
	     polearm - kit of a polearm it carries besides its weapon (warriors). It takes the polearm out when
	               monsters surround it, so its normal attacks hit several of them, and switches back to its
	               weapon once most of them are dead (see FakePvpPolearm* in config/Custom/FakePlayerPvp.ini).
	               A build whose weapon is a polearm (Dreadnought) always has its multi-attack.
	     weight  - relative chance to pick this build.
	     skillFighter - true for a class that deals its damage with skills (Gladiator/Duelist, Tyrant,
	               daggers): it uses a skill most of the time (FakePvpSkillChance). The others (tanks,
	               archers, most warriors) fight with their normal attack and use a skill now and then
	               (FakePvpAutoAttackSkillChance); mages always cast.
	     Skills are lists of skill ids. The level of each skill (and whether the fake player
	     has it at all) comes from the class skill tree for its level, like a real character.
	     "a|b|c" means only the first learned one is used (e.g. exclusive totems).
	     attack    - damage skills, most preferred first.
	     debuff    - stuns, roots and debuffs (mostly used against players).
	     buff      - self buffs kept up while fighting.
	     heal      - self heals.
	     emergency - used below 30% HP.
	     toggle    - toggles switched on at spawn.
	     charge    - skills that build Sonic/Force energy (Duelist, Tyrant). Energy is spent by the energy
	                 skills like a player's, so they charge up between and during fights.
	     move      - short speed buffs used to catch a player that gets away, or to run away (Dash, Sonic Move).
	     rush      - gap closers used on a target out of reach (Rush, Shadow Step).
	     peel      - skills that stop a player in melee range: archers and mages use them before stepping
	                 back, and a fake player running away uses them on its pursuer (roots, stuns, Aura Flash, Trick).
	                 The first one that reaches the player from where it stands is used (a melee stun only once it is on it).
	     cleanse   - skills that remove what holds it back, only used when it has it (Break Duress, Remedy...).
	     summon    - servitor summons, "a|b" for the one to use (e.g. Summon Reanimated Man). It spawns with its servitor out,
	                 which fights what it fights. When the servitor dies in a PvP it runs off, summons a new one where it
	                 is safe (the cast is 15 seconds, and it runs on when a player catches up) and goes back to the fight.
	     link      - toggles switched on with the servitor and off when it dies (Transfer Pain: part of the damage it
	                 takes goes to the servitor).
	     combo     - skill chains played in order, like a practiced player's rotation. The first one that is
	                 ready (required steps learned and off cooldown, enough energy) starts.
	                 pvp="true": only against players. chance: % to start it when ready (default 100).
	                 step attributes:
	                   optional       - skipped when it can't be used right now (otherwise it is waited for)
	                   self           - cast on itself (buff before the burst)
	                   behind         - get behind the target first (Backstab, Lethal Blow)
	                   disabledTarget - only while the target is stunned, asleep, paralyzed or rooted
	                 A debuff that is already on the target is skipped, and so is a self buff when it, or any
	                 buff of the same type, is already on (e.g. Focus Chance/Power/Death replace each other).
	     Class passive skills (masteries, etc.) for the level are always added.
-->
